# Workstreams

## WS-A: State and defect geometry

Owns exact-zero vacua, nonzero-defect critical points, relative equilibria,
strata, admissible tangent cones, intrinsic Hessians, Witten repair, and
stability.

## WS-B: First-order dynamics

Owns the closure charge, superconnection, adjoint, complex/real structures,
inner curved differential, reversible flow, dissipative repair, and phase
retention.

## WS-C: Central extension and finite carriers

Owns the shared centre, finite cyclic quotients, Heisenberg-Weyl relations,
Fourier/Clifford automorphisms, Heisenberg-Nil transfer, tensor carriers,
center/commutant reduction, and scalar identifiability.

## WS-D: Categorical preprojection language

Owns nested admissibility germs, restricted morphisms, equivalence, descent,
curved homological transfer, functors, and the meaning of `same source` up to a
declared derived or Morita equivalence.

## WS-E: Existing-theory bridges

Read-only consumers of promoted MTT results. Each bridge is a commuting diagram
with explicit source, target, retained data, lost data, and error contract.

## WS-F: Physical discrimination

Owns parameter counting, scale setting, RG/matching, unused predictions, and
falsification. A representation match is not a physical success in this stream.

## Parallelism

WS-A, WS-B, and WS-C can proceed independently. WS-D starts from their minimal
common interface. WS-E waits for a stable WS-D definition. WS-F begins only
after at least one typed physical bridge exists.
